# Raw market data is committed (was gitignored until 2026-07-31) so the repo can
# be cloned and worked on elsewhere without re-pulling from Dukascopy. Note the
# tradeoff (see CLAUDE.md s0.4): parquet is binary, so git keeps every version
# with no delta compression and the history grows on re-pulls. The fetcher stays
# idempotent, so re-pulling remains the alternative if the history gets heavy.

# `logs/*` (not `logs/`) so a specific file below can be re-included — git
# cannot un-ignore a file whose parent DIRECTORY is ignored.
logs/*
# ...except the holdout access log: it is the audit trail of how many times the
# holdout has been read, which is what makes pre-registration meaningful (s2).
!logs/holdout_access.log

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/*.ipynb
